      "problem": "$3+\\frac{3}{2}x-1-\\frac{7}{4}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+\\frac{3x}{2}-1-\\frac{7x}{4} & = \\\\ (\\frac{3x}{2}-\\frac{7x}{4})+(3-1) & = \\\\ (\\frac{6}{4}-\\frac{7}{4})x+(3-1) & = \\\\ (\\frac{6-7}{4})x+2 & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
